{offset205}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

Imperial Palace of Fanazaki{offset0}







The emperor Tagamoshi is saved but Goziya has fled Fanazaki on board his admiral battleship: the "Gozamato", there's no doubt about his destination, heading towards his fief, {arialbld}Goziyama.{arial}

Somebody had better drag this old seadog out of his lair before he finds the time to reorganise his forces.{pause}

That somebody is you, {rank} {name}, and you alone!{pause}

From my side, I'm going to keep those Katzarin hounds at bay. Rumor has it the Katzar-Khat will launch an attack in person...

You will be confronting Goziya at sea, his favorite terrain, you can be sure he is anticipating this battle with the utmost excitement. 

Goziya disposes of battleship technology, the Gozamoto is a "striking" example. Imagine a floating fortress equipped with steel battlements surmounted by 12-inch long range parts, all of which can displace at a speed of 24 knots. (see below for a picture of the thing){pause}











{center}{device24}











{pause}Our cruisers can't measure up against these Juggernauts anymore than a nail file can pierce into a granite tunnel. As far as firepower goes, the Gozamoto alone can turn anything you build less than 3 miles from its sides into a smoking crater.

So now you get it, you're about to take a suicide mission. If you haven't written to your parents recently I recommend you do it now.{pause}

I think only a submarine can give you a minimal chance of getting rid of the Gozamato. Still you will not leave for this mission without the latest gadget born from Schyzo expertise... 
We have made great progress in rocket technology, their range and power make them a decisive weapon. Our cruisers can be upgraded with a new type of rocket-launching turrets conceived especially for them.{pause}

Let's hope intensive shooting of these fireworks will stop the Gozamato.


{offset150}{arialbld}Tyron Spirex{arial}

